                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Unoptimized mess where you need to jump through hoops just to prevent it from crashing immediately. I was drawn in by the papercraft artstyle, but the lack of differing line weights makes it hard to tell apart backgrounds from collectables. Speaking of collectables, there is no point in collecting them, theyre impossible to find and then only happen to unlock empty rooms that look identical to all the other rooms. No substance in any them, your reward is nothing. That's how the entire game can be described as, having no substance. It's charming to see all the creative energy that went into this, it's an attractive game, but more time should have been put into the actual game aspect of it.",
